In what is seen, wrap every element named from the list above in backticks — `林` waits on the platform — because a backticked name is the picture the shot's frame is drawn with, listed in the order the names appear; a name not wrapped is prose and carries no picture. Every shot that happens in a place must name its act's place from the scene list in backticks, unless it is a close-up (shotSize close or extremeClose) or truly shows no place: a frame drawn without its place loses the film's world. Every character who speaks in a shot must be named in backticks in that shot's content, whoever else the shot shows, so the frame carries the face the line belongs to.

